Reads /proc/self/maps to count live memory mappings directly, which exists
only on Linux — macOS has no /proc filesystem and no in-language equivalent
this program could read instead (vmmap is an external tool with no argv/output
capture path available to a running Bit program; see #2167's ticket comment
for the manual macOS proof via `vmmap | grep -c VM_ALLOCATE`, run by hand
against this exact repro shape). The stress harness skips any directory
containing this marker on a Darwin host.
